---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Organic Lollipops: What to Look for on the Label"
  description="Not all organic lollipops are equal. Here's what actually matters when choosing organic fruit candy for your family or your store."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": "Organic Lollipops: What to Look for on the Label",
    "description": "Not all organic lollipops are equal. Here's what actually matters when choosing organic fruit candy for your family or your store.",
    "datePublished": "2025-01-01",
    "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "YumEarth EU" },
    "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "YumEarth EU", "logo": { "@type": "ImageObject", "url": "https://yumearth.eu/images/yumearth-logo.png" } },
    "mainEntityOfPage": { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": "https://yumearth.eu/blog/organic-lollipops" }
  })} />
  <Nav />
  <main class="pt-32 pb-24">
    <article class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
        <a href="/blog" class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest" style="color:var(--color-teal);">← Blog</a>
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest px-3 py-1 rounded-full" style="background:rgba(0,122,133,0.10); color:var(--color-teal);">Products</span>
        <span class="text-xs" style="color:var(--color-ink-muted);">2025</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="font-black mb-6" style="font-family:'ClashDisplay','Nunito',sans-serif; font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem); line-height:1.0; letter-spacing:-0.03em;">
        Organic Lollipops: What to Look for on the Label
      </h1>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-base" style="color:var(--color-ink); line-height:1.75;">
        <p class="text-xl font-medium" style="color:var(--color-ink-muted); line-height:1.65; max-width:65ch;">The organic candy market has grown fast. Not every product with "organic" on the label is made the same way. Here's what actually matters when you're choosing organic fruit candy.</p>
        <h2 class="font-black text-xl mt-10 mb-2" style="font-family:'ClashDisplay','Nunito',sans-serif; letter-spacing:-0.02em;">Look for the certification, not just the word</h2>
        <p style="max-width:65ch;">"Organic" on a package means nothing without a certification body behind it. In the US, that's USDA Organic. In the EU, it's the EU Organic logo. Without one of these, the claim isn't regulated. YumEarth carries USDA Organic certification — one of the highest standards globally.</p>
        <h2 class="font-black text-xl mt-10 mb-2" style="font-family:'ClashDisplay','Nunito',sans-serif; letter-spacing:-0.02em;">Colors: fruit juice or synthetic dye?</h2>
        <p style="max-width:65ch;">A candy can be organic but still use synthetic colorants. FD&C dyes like Red 40 and Yellow 5 are not allowed under USDA Organic certification, but some brands use "natural" dyes that are still chemically extracted. YumEarth uses organic fruit and vegetable juice concentrates — strawberry, carrot, purple sweet potato, turmeric — as both colorants and flavor contributors.</p>
        <h2 class="font-black text-xl mt-10 mb-2" style="font-family:'ClashDisplay','Nunito',sans-serif; letter-spacing:-0.02em;">Allergen profile</h2>
        <p style="max-width:65ch;">Organic doesn't automatically mean allergen-free. Check for wheat, soy, tree nuts, and dairy — common in organic candy processing. YumEarth lollipops are free from the top 9 allergens, making them one of the few organic fruit candies safe for classrooms and kids with multiple restrictions.</p>
        <h2 class="font-black text-xl mt-10 mb-2" style="font-family:'ClashDisplay','Nunito',sans-serif; letter-spacing:-0.02em;">Ingredient count</h2>
        <p style="max-width:65ch;">A short ingredient list is usually a good sign. YumEarth Classic Lollipops contain: organic cane sugar, organic tapioca syrup, citric acid, organic fruit and vegetable juice (color), natural flavors, vitamin C. Six to eight ingredients. You can read every one of them.</p>
        <h2 class="font-black text-xl mt-10 mb-2" style="font-family:'ClashDisplay','Nunito',sans-serif; letter-spacing:-0.02em;">Where to buy organic lollipops in Europe</h2>
        <p style="max-width:65ch;">YumEarth is distributed across 40+ countries in Europe, the Middle East, and Central Asia. If you're a retailer looking to stock organic lollipops or organic fruit candy, contact us for wholesale pricing and availability in your market.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-16 rounded-3xl p-10" style="background:var(--color-surface);">
        <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest mb-3" style="color:var(--color-teal);">USDA Organic certified</p>
        <h3 class="font-black mb-3" style="font-family:'ClashDisplay','Nunito',sans-serif; font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem); letter-spacing:-0.03em;">The organic lollipop standard.</h3>
        <p class="text-base mb-6" style="color:var(--color-ink-muted); line-height:1.65; max-width:480px;">14 flavors. Real fruit colors. No artificial anything. Available wholesale across Europe & the Middle East.</p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="/lollipops" class="btn-primary text-sm">See lollipops →</a>
          <a href="/contact" class="btn-secondary text-sm">Wholesale enquiry</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
